# NIP-05 discovery must stay cross-origin readable for Nostr clients.
/.well-known/nostr.json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Content-Type: application/json

# ⚠️ THE MACHINE ROUTES ARE noindex — AND THIS DOES NOT MAKE THEM LESS AVAILABLE
# TO AGENTS, which is the whole point of this site's crawlability work.
# `X-Robots-Tag: noindex` is a directive to SEARCH INDEXERS. It is NOT a crawl
# block: these routes still serve 200 with their full body to anyone who asks,
# robots.txt still welcomes every named AI crawler, /llms.txt still indexes all
# 394 entries, and every article page still advertises its twin via rel=alternate.
# The ONLY thing it removes is Google keeping a second copy of the encyclopedia.
#
# Why it was needed (measured 2026-08-07 against Search Console + the live site):
# every article links `/wiki/<slug>.md`, so the site presents ~800 crawlable URLs
# for 394 real articles, and nothing tells Google the two halves are the same
# thing — a .md file cannot carry an HTML <link rel=canonical>, so an HTTP header
# is the only place that signal can live. Search Console showed 399 of 400 URLs
# sitting in "Discovered - currently not indexed": Google had found the site and
# was rationing how much of it to fetch. Handing a 16-day-old domain a crawl
# surface twice the size of its actual content spends that ration on duplicates.
#
# NOTE: `/*.md` matches NESTED paths, so this one rule covers every /wiki/*.md
# twin. Verified on bitcoineconomy.ai, which documents the same behaviour in its
# own _headers. Cloudflare applies EVERY matching rule cumulatively and CONCATENATES
# values for repeated headers — so never add a second block for a path listed here.
/*.md
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/llms.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/llms-full.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
